  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "slug": "imam-bayildi-term",
      "term": "Imam bayildi",
      "definition": "A Turkish dish of whole aubergines stuffed with onion, garlic and tomato in olive oil; the name means the imam fainted, said to be from the extravagance of the olive oil used."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": [],
  "criticalTechniques": [],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 4 and takes around 20 minutes to prepare and 55 minutes to cook. Whole aubergines are split, salted, then filled with a deeply savoury onion, garlic and tomato mixture before a long, slow bake in plenty of olive oil. The result is silky and rich, served at room temperature as a meze or a light main."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: do not skimp on the olive oil here. The aubergines absorb it during baking and it is what gives the dish its characteristic soft, luxurious texture. Use the best quality olive oil you have."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
