      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oven to 180C (Fan 160C / Gas 4). Cut the aubergines in half lengthways and score the flesh in a crosshatch, taking care not to cut through the skin. Sprinkle generously with salt and leave for 10 minutes, then pat dry with kitchen paper."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Warm 60ml of the olive oil in the frying pan over a medium heat. Fry the aubergines cut-side down for 5 minutes until golden. Transfer them to the rectangular baking tin cut-side up."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In the same pan, cook the onion in another 30ml olive oil over a low heat for 12 minutes until soft and golden. Add the garlic and cook for 2 more minutes, then stir in the tomato, cinnamon and black pepper. Cook for 5 minutes until the tomato softens into a loose sauce."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove from the heat and stir in half the parsley. Spoon the filling generously into each aubergine half, pressing it into the scored flesh."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour the remaining olive oil and the lemon juice over and around the aubergines. Add a splash of water to the base of the tin (about 60ml) to create steam during baking."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cover the tin tightly with foil and bake for 40 minutes. Remove the foil and bake for a further 15 minutes until the aubergines are completely tender and the tops are lightly coloured."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Leave to cool to room temperature. Scatter over the remaining parsley and serve with crusty bread or rice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Aubergines are bitter"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Salt the cut flesh and leave for at least 10 minutes before cooking. This draws out moisture and any residual bitterness. Pat thoroughly dry before frying."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Filling is watery"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cook the tomato filling until most of the liquid has evaporated before spooning it into the aubergines. A wet filling makes the dish soggy."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Aubergines not soft after baking"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make sure the foil is sealed tightly for the first 40 minutes. The steam trapped inside is what cooks the flesh through. If they are still firm, cover and return for another 10 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This is one of the great dishes of the Ottoman kitchen, known across Turkey simply as "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "imam-bayildi-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "imam bayildi"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". It appears at almost every meze spread in Turkish homes and restaurants. The combination of slowly softened onion, tomato and garlic soaked into the aubergine flesh is deeply satisfying. Served at room temperature, it actually improves as it sits and the flavours settle. A squeeze of lemon just before serving lifts the whole dish."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}